    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5a10d5ac-d229-5645-bc2d-269831468be8",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - y + 2 z &=4 \\\\ 3 x - 2 y + 6 z &=10 \\\\ - 2 x + 2 y - z &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & 10 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -1 & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & 10 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -1 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -1 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
